{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py` sits at the reconciler package root but\nIS Jira adapter code: it implements `_map_jira_to_local_fields`, which\n`adapters/jira/backend.py` (`_JiraInbound.map_remote_to_local`) and\n`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` (`_DCInbound.map_remote_to_local`) delegate to, and it\nlazy-loads `adapters/jira/adf.py` by path under the literal key\n`\"rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira.adf\"`. It stayed at root during epic bbf1's S5 relocation for\nloader location-pinning reasons and is the single recorded exemption in the neutrality sweep\ngate (`_SWEEP_EXEMPTIONS = {\"inbound_fields.py\"}`,\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py:362`). Relocating it into\n`adapters/jira/` completes vendor-code residency and lets that exemption be deleted.\n\n## Approach\n\n`git mv` the module to `adapters/jira/inbound_fields.py` and update every reference atomically\n(the S5 recipe, change 905). No re-export shim at the old path (S5 policy: no shims).\n\nReference set, established by BOTH Serena `find_referencing_symbols` and a raw grep for the\nmodule name as a STRING (to catch `importlib`/by-path loaders the LSP cannot see):\n\n1. **The moved module's own loader.** `_load_adf` computes\n   `Path(__file__).parent / \"adapters\" / \"jira\" / \"adf.py\"`. After the move `__file__`'s parent\n   IS `adapters/jira/`, so the path becomes `Path(__file__).parent / \"adf.py\"`. The inline\n   `spec_from_file_location` loader and the `_ADF_KEY_INBOUND` sys.modules key are kept\n   unchanged — the module is still loaded by path (with no package context) by\n   `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_unmapped_status_no_reopen.py`, so a\n   relative import would break it.\n2. **Production importers** — rewrite `rebar_reconciler.inbound_fields` to\n   `rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira.inbound_fields`:\n   - `adapters/jira/backend.py:21` (`from rebar_reconciler import inbound_fields`)\n   - `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:132,137` (function-local imports)\n   - `inbound_differ.py:36` (the re-export block)\n   - `peer_state.py:34` (`normalize_baseline_value`)\n   - `scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py:68`, `scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py:24`\n3. **Test importers / by-path + by-string loaders:**\n   - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py:182,515`\n   - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_inbound_update_assignee_mint_5200.py:80,162`\n   - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_parent_clear_88d9.py:438`\n     (`importlib.import_module(\"rebar_reconciler.inbound_fields\")` — a STRING the LSP cannot see)\n   - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_unmapped_status_no_reopen.py:40`\n     (`_INBOUND_FIELDS_PATH`, a filesystem path)\n   - `tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py:669` (`_recon(\"inbound_fields\")`)\n4. **Structural-gate bookkeeping:**\n   - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py` — delete `_SWEEP_EXEMPTIONS` and\n     its use, and delete `test_sweep_exemption_is_still_needed` (which asserts the exempted file\n     still carries the literal; once the file is out of the package root that assertion is\n     meaningless, and it would fail on a missing path). The sweep\n     (`test_no_root_core_module_carries_vendor_lazyload_literal`) then runs with ZERO exemptions.\n   - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py:221` — the `_ADF_ALLOWLIST` key\n     is a path relative to the reconciler root, so `\"inbound_fields.py\"` becomes\n     `\"adapters/jira/inbound_fields.py\"`.\n\nChecked and deliberately NOT changed:\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py`'s `_PINNED_PATHS` contains\n  only `adapters/jira/{adf,outbound_fields,comment_limits}.py`; `inbound_fields.py` is not\n  location-pinned, so no pinning gate is affected.\n- `_ZERO_ADAPTER_IMPORT_SCALAR_CORE` in the neutrality gate does not list `inbound_differ.py` or\n  `peer_state.py`, so those two root modules importing `adapters.jira.inbound_fields` breaks no\n  gate. (Removing that last root->vendor import edge is separate, later work — it is the\n  injected-`InboundMapper` path that ticket 4af8 started; out of scope here.)\n- `docs/adr/0035-reconciler-vendor-adapter-seam.md` names the module (`inbound_fields`), not a\n  path, and is a point-in-time decision record; left as-is.\n- Prose-only mentions in comments/docstrings that name the module without importing it\n  (`_backend.py:412`, `reconcile_check.py:203`, `adapters/jira_datacenter/_people.py:87`,\n  `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py`, `test_backend_characterization.py`) stay\n  accurate because the module NAME is unchanged.\n\nRejected alternative: a re-export shim at the old path (S5 policy: no shims).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py` -> `adapters/jira/inbound_fields.py`\n  (+ its own `_load_adf` path)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py`,\n  `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py`, `inbound_differ.py`, `peer_state.py`\n- `scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py`, `scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py`\n- the five test files listed above, plus `test_backend_neutrality.py` and\n  `test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nThis is a behavior-preserving relocation, so the proof is that the existing suite still passes\nwith every reference repointed, plus the gate that exists BECAUSE the file was misplaced now\npassing with its exemption deleted:\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py::test_no_root_core_module_carries_vendor_lazyload_literal`\n  is the load-bearing test: it runs with `_SWEEP_EXEMPTIONS` removed entirely, so it fails if the\n  file is still (or again) at the package root. That is the direct proof the move is complete.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_unmapped_status_no_reopen.py` proves the\n  by-path load still works from the new location (it is the standalone `spec_from_file_location`\n  consumer, and it exercises `_load_adf`'s repointed sibling path).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_parent_clear_88d9.py::` the\n  `importlib.import_module` consumer check proves the dotted module path resolves.\nNo NEW test is written: the relocation adds no behavior, and the existing gate — with the\nexemption deleted — is a sharper oracle than any new assertion would be.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py` no longer exists and\n      `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/inbound_fields.py` does; verified by\n      `test -e`/`test ! -e` and by `git log --follow` showing a rename, with NO shim module left\n      at the old path.\n- [ ] No reference to the old dotted path survives; checked by\n      `git grep -n 'rebar_reconciler\\.inbound_fields' -- src tests scripts` exiting non-zero, and\n      `git grep -n \"rebar_reconciler\\\" / \\\"inbound_fields.py\\\"\\|/ \\\"inbound_fields.py\\\"\" -- tests`\n      showing only the new `adapters/jira` path.\n- [ ] `_SWEEP_EXEMPTIONS` is gone from `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py`\n      (`git grep -n _SWEEP_EXEMPTIONS -- tests` exits non-zero) and\n      `test_no_root_core_module_carries_vendor_lazyload_literal` passes with zero exemptions.\n- [ ] `test_sweep_exemption_is_still_needed` is deleted (it asserted the exemption was still\n      needed; it is not).\n- [ ] `make lint && make typecheck && make test` green with the worktree venv on PATH."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786096799154423001,"uuid":"b0974f14-6495-4fec-8e1c-b52a6c759896"}